185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 132 0 R
/E (This study adopts a qualitative, exploratory, and interpretive research design to investigate the social and cultural normalization of online gambling among young adults in Portugal. Qualitative research is uniquely suited for this study as it is designed to explore the behavioral processes and cognitive rationalizations that drive consumer behavior \(Gainsbury, 2015\). Rather than measuring statistics, this approach seeks to interpret real-world phenomena through the lived experiences and opinions of the participants. By gathering data directly through one-on-one interactions, we captured rich, detailed perspectives on how gambling integrates into the daily lives of the target demographic. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
