<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (No specific targeting was used regarding gender or gambling frequency; instead, these variables distributed naturally through fallout. The core inclusion criteria required participants to be between 18 and 36 years old and currently residing in Portugal. However, the final sample comprised 47 participants \(aged 20 to 36\) with a balanced split of approximately 50% active gamblers and 50% non-gamblers. This approach captured the internal behavioral processes of users alongside the external social perceptions, peer pressures, and environmental exposure observed by non-gamblers. The sample distributed naturally at approximately 40% female and 60% male. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
