192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (Data collection was executed within an academic window between May 5 and May 10. Prior to the official interviews, the script was refined under the guidance of the professor and pre-tested with individuals from the target demographic to ensure clarity, flow, and neutrality, preventing potential interviewer bias. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (All 47 interviews were conducted remotely via Microsoft Teams using institutional Nova IMS accounts to leverage the platform's automated transcription tool. This sample size aligns with recommendations for thematic saturation in qualitative research, where saturation typically occurs between 12 and 30 interviews for homogeneous populations \(Guest, Bunce & Johnson, 2006\). Sessions lasted from 15 minutes to 1 hour, with a mean duration of 30 minutes, following a standardized protocol: )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 525 0 R
/E (The interviewer explicitly stated the academic purpose of the study and guaranteed strict data confidentiality.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 526 0 R
/E (The interviewer formally announced that the session was being recorded for academic purposes. The participant provided explicit verbal consent on the record before any questions began.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 527 0 R
/E (The semi-structured script was applied flexibly, moving from broader environmental aspects \(advertising, football culture\) to specific personal mechanics \(payment methods, risk signals, and biometric innovations\). )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
